ation helpers:\\n\\n```tsx\\nimport { useTypedTranslation } from \'@/hooks/useTranslation\';\\n\\nfunction MyComponent() {\\n  const { tButton, tLabel, tMessage, tNav } = useTypedTranslation();\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      <h1>{tMessage(\'welcome\')}</h1>\\n      <button>{tButton(\'save\')}</button>\\n      <label>{tLabel(\'email\')}</label>\\n      <nav>{tNav(\'home\')}</nav>\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Language Management\\n\\n### Language Switching\\n\\nUse the `useLanguage` hook to manage language settings:\\n\\n```tsx\\nimport { useLanguage } from \'@/providers/i18n-provider\';\\nimport { I18N_LANGUAGES } from \'@/i18n/config\';\\n\\nfunction LanguageSwitcher() {\\n  const { language, changeLanguage } = useLanguage();\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      <p>Current: {language.name}</p>\\n      {I18N_LANGUAGES.map((lang) => (\\n        <button\\n          key={lang.code}\\n          onClick={() => changeLanguage(lang.code)}\\n          className={language.code === lang.code ? \'active\' : \'\'}\\n        >\\n          <img src={lang.flag} alt={lang.name} />\\n          {lang.shortName}\\n        </button>\\n      ))}\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Available Languages\\n\\nThe following languages are supported out of the box:\\n\\n| Language | Code | Direction | Flag |\\n|----------|------|-----------|------|\\n| English | `en` | LTR | \uD83C\uDDFA\uD83C\uDDF8 |\\n| Arabic | `ar` | RTL | \uD83C\uDDF8\uD83C\uDDE6 |\\n| Spanish | `es` | LTR | \uD83C\uDDEA\uD83C\uDDF8 |\\n| German | `de` | LTR | \uD83C\uDDE9\uD83C\uDDEA |\\n| Chinese | `ch` | LTR | \uD83C\uDDE8\uD83C\uDDF3 |\\n\\n## Translation Keys Structure\\n\\nTranslation files are organized in a nested structure for better maintainability:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"common\\": {\\n    \\"buttons\\": {\\n      \\"save\\": \\"Save\\",\\n      \\"cancel\\": \\"Cancel\\",\\n      \\"delete\\": \\"Delete\\"\\n    },\\n    \\"labels\\": {\\n      \\"name\\": \\"Name\\",\\n      \\"email\\": \\"Email\\"\\n    },\\n    \\"messages\\": {\\n      \\"welcome\\": \\"Welcome\\",\\n      \\"loading\\": \\"Loading...\\",\\n      \\"success\\": \\"Operation completed successfully\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\"pages\\": {\\n    \\"home\\": {\\n      \\"title\\": \\"Home\\",\\n      \\"description\\": \\"Welcome to our application\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\"navigation\\": {\\n    \\"home\\": \\"Home\\",\\n    \\"settings\\": \\"Settings\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Advanced Features\\n\\n### Translation with Parameters\\n\\nSupport for dynamic content using interpolation:\\n\\n```tsx\\nconst { t } = useTranslation();\\nconst userName = \'John\';\\nconst count = 5;\\n\\nreturn (\\n  <div>\\n    <p>{t(\'Hello {{name}}!\', { name: userName })}</p>\\n    <p>{t(\'You have {{count}} messages\', { count })}</p>\\n  </div>\\n);\\n```\\n\\n### Pluralization\\n\\nHandle singular and plural forms:\\n\\n```tsx\\nconst { t } = useTranslation();\\nconst itemCount = 3;\\n\\nreturn <p>{t(\'item\', { count: itemCount })}</p>;\\n```\\n\\nAdd pluralization rules to your translation files:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"item_one\\": \\"{{count}} item\\",\\n  \\"item_other\\": \\"{{count}} items\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Namespaces\\n\\nOrganize translations using namespaces:\\n\\n```tsx\\nconst { t } = useTranslation(\'dashboard\');\\n\\nreturn <h1>{t(\'title\')}</h1>; // Looks for dashboard.title\\n```\\n\\n## Helper Functions\\n\\n### Available Helpers\\n\\nThe `useTypedTranslation` hook provides convenient helper functions:\\n\\n```tsx\\nconst { tButton, tLabel, tMessage, tNav } = useTypedTranslation();\\n\\n// Equivalent to:\\n// t(\'common.buttons.save\')\\ntButton(\'save\');\\n\\n// t(\'common.labels.email\')\\ntLabel(\'email\');\\n\\n// t(\'common.messages.welcome\')\\ntMessage(\'welcome\');\\n\\n// t(\'navigation.home\')\\ntNav(\'home\');\\n```\\n\\n## RTL Support\\n\\n### Automatic Direction Handling\\n\\nThe system automatically handles text direction based on the selected language:\\n\\n- **LTR Languages**: English, Spanish, German, Chinese\\n- **RTL Languages**: Arabic\\n\\n### CSS Considerations\\n\\nWhen styling for RTL support, use logical properties or direction-specific selectors:\\n\\n```css\\n/* Logical properties (recommended) */\\n.element {\\n  margin-inline-start: 1rem;\\n  padding-inline-end: 2rem;\\n}\\n\\n/* Direction-specific styles */\\n[dir=\\"rtl\\"] .element {\\n  text-align: right;\\n}\\n\\n[dir=\\"ltr\\"] .element {\\n  text-align: left;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Adding New Languages\\n\\n### Step 1: Create Translation File\\n\\nCreate a new JSON file in `i18n/messages/`:\\n\\n```bash\\n# Example: French translations\\ntouch i18n/messages/fr.json\\n```\\n\\n### Step 2: Add Language Configuration\\n\\nUpdate `i18n/config.ts`:\\n\\n```tsx\\nexport const I18N_LANGUAGES: Language[] = [\\n  // ... existing languages\\n  {\\n    code: \'fr\',\\n    name: \'French\',\\n    shortName: \'FR\',\\n    direction: \'ltr\',\\n    flag: \'/media/flags/france.svg\',\\n  },\\n];\\n```\\n\\n### Step 3: Import Translations\\n\\nUpdate `providers/i18n-provider.tsx`:\\n\\n```tsx\\nimport frTranslations from \'@/i18n/messages/fr.json\';\\n\\nconst resources = {\\n  // ... existing resources\\n  fr: { translation: frTranslations },\\n};\\n```\\n\\n## Best Practices\\n\\n### 1. Key Organization\\n\\n- Use descriptive, hierarchical keys\\n- Group related translations under common namespaces\\n- Keep keys consistent across all language files\\n\\n### 2. Avoid Hardcoded Strings\\n\\n```tsx\\n// ❌ Don\'t do this\\n<button>Save</button>\\n\\n// ✅ Do this\\n<button>{t(\'common.buttons.save\')}</button>\\n```\\n\\n### 3. Handle Missing Translations\\n\\nAlways provide fallback values:\\n\\n```tsx\\n// Provide fallback text\\n{t(\'some.key\', \'Default text\')}\\n\\n// Or use the helper with fallback\\n{tButton(\'save\') || \'Save\'}\\n```\\n\\n### 4. Test with Different Languages\\n\\n- Test UI with longer text (German) and shorter text (Chinese)\\n- Verify RTL layout with Arabic\\n- Check text overflow and wrapping\\n\\n### 5. Use Semantic Keys\\n\\n```tsx\\n// ❌ Don\'t use generic keys\\n{t(\'text1\')}\\n\\n// ✅ Use semantic keys\\n{t(\'pages.dashboard.welcome_message\')}\\n```\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n### Development Testing\\n\\nVisit the test page to see all features in action:\\n\\n```bash\\n# Navigate to the test page\\nhttp://localhost:3000/i18n-test\\n```\\n\\nThe test page includes:\\n- Basic translation examples\\n- Parameter interpolation\\n- Language switching\\n- RTL/LTR direction changes\\n- Debugging information\\n\\n### Manual Testing Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Language switching works correctly\\n- [ ] Translations display properly in all languages\\n- [ ] RTL layout works with Arabic\\n- [ ] Language preference persists after page reload\\n- [ ] Parameters and pluralization work\\n- [ ] No console errors or warnings\\n\\n## Troubleshooting\\n\\n### Common Issues\\n\\n**\\"useTranslation: You will need to pass in an i18next instance\\"**\\n- This error occurs when i18next isn\'t properly initialized\\n- Ensure the `I18nProvider` wraps your app in the layout\\n\\n**Missing translations showing as keys**\\n- Check that the translation key exists in all language files\\n- Verify the key path is correct (case-sensitive)\\n\\n**RTL layout not working**\\n- Ensure your CSS uses logical properties or direction selectors\\n- Check that `dir` attribute is set on the `<html>` element\\n\\n**Language not persisting**\\n- Verify localStorage is available and working\\n- Check browser developer tools for localStorage entries\\n\\n### Debug Information\\n\\nAccess debug information in development:\\n\\n```tsx\\nimport { useTranslation } from \'@/hooks/useTranslation\';\\n\\nfunction DebugInfo() {\\n  const { i18n } = useTranslation();\\n\\n  console.log(\'Current language:\', i18n.language);\\n  console.log(\'Available languages:\', i18n.languages);\\n  console.log(\'Loaded resources:\', Object.keys(i18n.store.data));\\n\\n  return null;\\n}