           <Toaster />\\n                  </TooltipsProvider>\\n                </I18nProvider>\\n              </ThemeProvider>\\n            </SettingsProvider>\\n          </AuthProvider>\\n        </QueryProvider>\\n      </body>\\n    </html>\\n  );\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Core Providers\\n\\n### Query Provider\\n\\nProvides TanStack Query functionality for data fetching and caching.\\n\\n**Usage:**\\n\\n```tsx\\n\'use client\';\\n\\nimport { useQuery } from \'@tanstack/react-query\';\\n\\nfunction UserProfile({ userId }: { userId: string }) {\\n  const { data, isLoading, error } = useQuery({\\n    queryKey: [\'user\', userId],\\n    queryFn: () => fetch(`/api/users/${userId}`).then(res => res.json())\\n  });\\n\\n  if (isLoading) return <div>Loading...</div>;\\n  if (error) return <div>Error loading user</div>;\\n\\n  return <div><h1>{data.name}</h1><p>{data.email}</p></div>;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Auth Provider\\n\\nWraps NextAuth.js SessionProvider to handle authentication state.\\n\\n**Usage:**\\n\\n```tsx\\n\'use client\';\\n\\nimport { useSession, signIn, signOut } from \'next-auth/react\';\\n\\nfunction LoginButton() {\\n  const { data: session } = useSession();\\n\\n  if (session) {\\n    return <button onClick={() => signOut()}>Sign out</button>;\\n  }\\n  return <button onClick={() => signIn()}>Sign in</button>;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Settings Provider\\n\\nManages application settings with localStorage persistence.\\n\\n**Usage:**\\n\\n```tsx\\n\'use client\';\\n\\nimport { useSettings } from \'@/providers/settings-provider\';\\n\\nfunction LayoutSettings() {\\n  const { getOption, storeOption } = useSettings();\\n\\n  // Get a setting\\n  const sidebarCollapsed = getOption(\'layouts.demo1.sidebarCollapse\');\\n\\n  // Update a setting (and save to localStorage)\\n  function toggleSidebar() {\\n    storeOption(\'layouts.demo1.sidebarCollapse\', !sidebarCollapsed);\\n  }\\n\\n  return <button onClick={toggleSidebar}>\\n    {sidebarCollapsed ? \'Expand\' : \'Collapse\'} Sidebar\\n  </button>;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Theme Provider\\n\\nManages dark/light mode using next-themes.\\n\\n**Usage:**\\n\\n```tsx\\n\'use client\';\\n\\nimport { useTheme } from \'next-themes\';\\n\\nfunction ThemeToggle() {\\n  const { theme, setTheme } = useTheme();\\n\\n  return (\\n    <button onClick={() => setTheme(theme === \'dark\' ? \'light\' : \'dark\')}>\\n      Switch to {theme === \'dark\' ? \'Light\' : \'Dark\'} Mode\\n    </button>\\n  );\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### I18n Provider\\n\\nManages internationalization and RTL support.\\n\\n**Usage:**\\n\\n```tsx\\n\'use client\';\\n\\nimport { useLanguage } from \'@/providers/i18n-provider\';\\nimport { I18N_LANGUAGES } from \'@/i18n/config\';\\n\\nfunction LanguageSelector() {\\n  const { languageCode, changeLanguage } = useLanguage();\\n\\n  return (\\n    <select\\n      value={languageCode}\\n      onChange={(e) => changeLanguage(e.target.value)}\\n    >\\n      {I18N_LANGUAGES.map(lang => (\\n        <option key={lang.code} value={lang.code}>\\n          {lang.name}\\n        </option>\\n      ))}\\n    </select>\\n  );\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Tooltips Provider\\n\\nProvides tooltip functionality for the application.\\n\\n**Usage:**\\n\\n```tsx\\n\'use client\';\\n\\nimport {\\n  Tooltip,\\n  TooltipContent,\\n  TooltipTrigger,\\n} from \'@/components/ui/tooltip\';\\n\\nfunction ButtonWithTooltip() {\\n  return (\\n    <Tooltip>\\n      <TooltipTrigger asChild>\\n        <button>Hover me</button>\\n      </TooltipTrigger>\\n      <TooltipContent>\\n        <p>Tooltip content</p>\\n      </TooltipContent>\\n    </Tooltip>\\n  );\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Creating Custom Hooks\\n\\nFor components that need access to multiple contexts, combine the hooks in a custom hook:\\n\\n```tsx\\n\'use client\';\\n\\nimport { useSettings } from \'@/providers/settings-provider\';\\nimport { useLanguage } from \'@/providers/i18n-provider\';\\nimport { useTheme } from \'next-themes\';\\n\\n// Custom hook combining multiple contexts\\nexport function useAppContext() {\\n  const settings = useSettings();\\n  const language = useLanguage();\\n  const theme = useTheme();\\n\\n  return { settings, language, theme };\\n}\\n\\n// Usage\\nfunction MyComponent() {\\n  const { settings, language, theme } = useAppContext();\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      <p>Current theme: {theme.theme}</p>\\n      <p>Current language: {language.languageCode}</p>\\n      <p>Layout: {settings.getOption(\'layout\')}</p>\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Provider-Specific Documentation\\n\\nFor more detailed information about each provider, refer to these guides:\\n\\n- [Authentication](/metronic-nextjs/guides/authentication) - Using the Auth Provider\\n- [Internationalization](/metronic-nextjs/guides/internationalization) - Using the I18n Provider\\n- [Dark Mode](/metronic-nextjs/guides/dark-mode) - Using the Theme Provider\\n- [RTL Support](/metronic-nextjs/guides/rtl) - RTL features with I18n Provider\\n","code":"var Component=(()=>{var p=Object.create;var o=Object.defineProperty;var E=Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor;var y=Object.getOwnPropertyNames;var m=Object.getPrototypeOf,u=Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty;var g=(l,e)=>()=>(e||l((e={exports:{}}).exports,e),e.exports),F=(l,e)=>{for(var s in e)o(l,s,{get:e[s],enumerable:!0})},i=(l,e,s,c)=>{if(e&&typeof e==\\"object\\"||typeof e==\\"function\\")for(let r of y(e))!u.call(l,r)&&r!==s&&o(l,r,{get:()=>e[r],enumerable:!(c=E(e,r))||c.enumerable});return l};var N=(l,e,s)=>(s=l!=null?p(m(l)):{},i(e||!l||!l.__esModule?o(s,\\"default\\",{value:l,enumerable:!0}):s,l)),v=l=>i(o({},\\"__esModule\\",{value:!0}),l);var t=g((C,a)=>{a.exports=_jsx_runtime});var B={};F(B,{default:()=>h,frontmatter:()=>x});var n=N(t()),x={title:\\"Providers\\",description:\\"Understanding and using context providers in Metronic Next.js\\"};function d(l){let e={a:\\"a\\",code:\\"code\\",div:\\"div\\",h1:\\"h1\\",h2:\\"h2\\",h3:\\"h3\\",li:\\"li\\",line:\\"line\\",p:\\"p\\",pre:\\"pre\\",span:\\"sp