com:5432/postgres\\"\\n\\n# Next Auth Config #\\nNEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000/api\\nNEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000/\\nNEXTAUTH_SECRET=your-nextauth-secret-key\\nGOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_google_oauth2_client_id\\nGOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your_google_oauth2_secret_key\\n\\n# Storage Configuration (AWS S3 or DigitalOcean Spaces)\\nSTORAGE_TYPE=digitalocean\\n\\nSTORAGE_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your_accent_key_id\\nSTORAGE_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your_access_key\\nSTORAGE_REGION=your_region\\nSTORAGE_BUCKET=your_bucket_name\\nSTORAGE_ENDPOINT=your_endpoint\\nSTORAGE_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true\\nSTORAGE_CDN_URL=your_cdn_url\\n\\n# SMTP Credentials\\nSMTP_HOST=your_smtp_host\\nSMTP_PORT=your_smtp_port\\nSMTP_SECURE=false\\nSMTP_USER=no-reply@domain.com\\nSMTP_PASS=your_smtp_pass\\n```\\n\\n### Database Setup\\n\\nThis project uses Prisma ORM to interact with the database. Set up your database with:\\n\\n```bash\\n# Generate Prisma client\\nnpx prisma generate\\n\\n# Run migrations (if needed)\\nnpx prisma migrate dev\\n```\\n\\n### Start the Development Server\\n\\nRun the development server:\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm run dev\\n```\\n\\nThe application will be available at:\\n```\\nhttp://localhost:3000\\n```\\n\\n### Build for Production\\n\\nWhen you\'re ready to deploy, build the application:\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm run build\\n```\\n\\nThe built files will be in the `.next` directory and can be deployed to any Next.js compatible hosting service.\\n\\n</Steps>\\n\\n## Project Structure\\n\\nThe Storely project follows a well-organized structure based on the App Router:\\n\\n```\\napp/                    # Next.js App Router directory\\n├── (auth)/             # Authentication routes (signin, signup, etc.)\\n├── (protected)/        # Protected routes requiring authentication\\n│   ├── account/        # Account settings pages\\n│   ├── page.tsx        # Dashboard page (default protected route)\\n│   └── layout.tsx      # Layout for protected routes\\n├── api/                # API routes\\n│   ├── auth/           # Authentication API endpoints\\n│   └── [...]/          # Other API endpoints\\n├── components/         # Shared UI components\\n│   ├── layouts/        # Multiple demo layouts (Demo1-Demo10)\\n│   └── ui/             # Base UI components\\n├── models/             # Data models and interfaces\\n└── layout.tsx          # Root layout component\\n\\ncomponents/             # Global UI components\\nconfig/                 # Configuration files\\ncss/                    # Global CSS styles\\nhooks/                  # Custom React hooks\\ni18n/                   # Internationalization files\\nlib/                    # Utility libraries\\nprisma/                 # Prisma schema and migrations\\nproviders/              # React context providers\\n├── auth-provider.tsx   # Authentication provider\\n├── i18n-provider.tsx   # Internationalization provider\\n├── query-provider.tsx  # TanStack Query provider\\n├── settings-provider.tsx # App settings provider\\n├── theme-provider.tsx  # Dark/light theme provider\\n└── tooltips-provider.tsx # Tooltips provider\\npublic/                 # Static assets (images, fonts, etc.)\\nservices/               # API service functions\\ntypes/                  # TypeScript type definitions\\n```\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n\\nAfter installation, you might want to:\\n\\n- Explore the [Adding a New Page](/storely/guides/adding-new-page) guide\\n- Learn about the [Authentication](/storely/guides/authentication) system\\n- Understand the [App Router](/storely/guides/routing) structure\\n- Check out the [Internationalization](/storely/guides/internationalization) features\\n- Experiment with different [Layouts](/storely/guides/layouts)\\n\\n## Troubleshooting\\n\\n### Common Issues\\n\\n1. **Port Already in Use**\\n\\nIf port 3000 is already in use, Next.js will automatically try to use the next available port. Check your terminal for the correct URL.\\n\\n2. **Missing Dependencies**\\n\\nIf you encounter errors about missing dependencies, try:\\n\\n```bash\\nnpm install --force\\n```\\n\\n3. **Database Connection Issues**\\n\\nIf you\'re having trouble connecting to your Supabase database, verify your `DATABASE_URL` and `DIRECT_URL` in the `.env` file. Make sure your Supabase project has the right permissions set.\\n\\n4. **Authentication Problems**\\n\\nFor authentication issues, check that your `NEXTAUTH_SECRET` and OAuth provider credentials are correctly set in the `.env` file.\\n\\n5. **Build Errors**\\n\\nIf you encounter build errors, ensure you\'re using the correct Node.js version (18+) and try clearing the node_modules directory:\\n\\n```bash\\nrm -rf node_modules .next\\nnpm install --force\\n```\\n\\nFor additional help, don\'t hesitate to contact us on our forum [devs.keenthemes.com](https://devs.keenthemes.com).","code":"var Component=(()=>{var p=Object.create;var t=Object.defineProperty;var u=Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor;var y=Object.getOwnPropertyNames;var g=Object.getPrototypeOf,m=Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty;var E=(l,e)=>()=>(e||l((e={exports:{}}).exports,e),e.exports),_=(l,e)=>{for(var r in e)t(l,r,{get:e[r],enumerable:!0})},o=(l,e,r,s)=>{if(e&&typeof e==\\"object\\"||typeof e==\\"function\\")for(let i of y(e))!m.call(l,i)&&i!==r&&t(l,i,{get:()=>e[i],enumerable:!(s=u(e,i))||s.enumerable});return l};var x=(l,e,r)=>(r=l!=null?p(g(l)):{},o(e||!l||!l.__esModule?t(r,\\"default\\",{value:l,enumerable:!0}):r,l)),f=l=>o(t({},\\"__esModule\\",{value:!0}),l);var c=E((S,a)=>{a.exports=_jsx_runtime});var C={};_(C,{default:()=>h,frontmatter:()=>F});var n=x(c()),F={title:\\"Installation\\",description:\\"Get started with Storely by following this installation guide.\\"};function d(l){let e={a:\\"a\\",code:\\"code\\",div:\\"div\\",h2:\\"h2\\",h3:\\"h3\\",li:\\"li\\",line:\\"line\\",ol:\\"ol\\",p:\\"p\\",pre:\\"pre\\",span:\\"span\\",strong:\\"strong\\",svg:\\"svg\\",ul:\\"ul\\",...l.components},{Steps:r}=e;return r||w(\\"Steps\\",!0),(0,n.jsxs)(n.Fragment,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(e.p,{chi