mdx","sourceFileName":"deployment.mdx","sourceFileDir":"supastart/(guides)","contentType":"mdx","flattenedPath":"supastart/(guides)/deployment"},"type":"Doc","slug":"/supastart/deployment","slugAsParams":"supastart/deployment","instance":"supastart"},{"title":"Internationalization (i18n)","description":"Learn how to use internationalization in Supastart.","published":true,"featured":false,"component":false,"toc":true,"body":{"raw":"\\n## Overview\\n\\nSupastart includes built-in internationalization (i18n) that enables your application to support multiple languages, RTL layouts, and locale-specific formatting.\\n\\n## Implementation\\n\\nSupastart\'s i18n system consists of:\\n\\n1. **i18next Integration** - For translations\\n2. **Language Provider** - For state management\\n3. **Formatting Utilities** - For dates, times, and currencies\\n4. **Translation Files** - JSON-based locale files\\n5. **RTL Support** - For right-to-left languages\\n\\n## Configuration\\n\\n### Core Setup\\n\\nThe i18n configuration is in `src/app/i18n.ts`:\\n\\n```typescript\\n// src/app/i18n.ts\\nimport arTranslation from \'@/i18n/messages/ar.json\';\\nimport chTranslation from \'@/i18n/messages/ch.json\';\\nimport deTranslation from \'@/i18n/messages/de.json\';\\nimport enTranslation from \'@/i18n/messages/en.json\';\\nimport esTranslation from \'@/i18n/messages/es.json\';\\nimport i18n from \'i18next\';\\nimport { initReactI18next } from \'react-i18next\';\\n\\ni18n.use(initReactI18next).init({\\n  resources: {\\n    en: { translation: enTranslation },\\n    ar: { translation: arTranslation },\\n    de: { translation: deTranslation },\\n    es: { translation: esTranslation },\\n    ch: { translation: chTranslation },\\n  },\\n  lng: \'en\',\\n  fallbackLng: \'en\',\\n  interpolation: { escapeValue: false },\\n});\\n\\nexport default i18n;\\n```\\n\\n### Language Settings\\n\\nLanguages are defined in `src/i18n/config.ts`:\\n\\n```typescript\\n// src/i18n/config.ts\\nexport const languages: Language[] = [\\n  {\\n    code: \'en\',\\n    name: \'English\',\\n    shortName: \'EN\',\\n    direction: \'ltr\',\\n    flag: \'/media/flags/united-states.svg\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    code: \'ar\',\\n    name: \'Arabic\',\\n    shortName: \'AR\',\\n    direction: \'rtl\',\\n    flag: \'/media/flags/saudi-arabia.svg\',\\n  },\\n  // Other languages...\\n];\\n```\\n\\n## Translation Files\\n\\nTranslation strings are stored as JSON files in `src/i18n/messages/`:\\n\\n```json\\n// src/i18n/messages/en.json (simplified)\\n{\\n  \\"common\\": {\\n    \\"messages\\": {\\n      \\"unauthorized\\": \\"Unauthorized access.\\",\\n      \\"system_error\\": \\"Oops! Something didn\'t go as planned.\\"\\n    },\\n    \\"logout\\": \\"Logout\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"login\\": {\\n    \\"title\\": \\"Login\\",\\n    \\"email\\": \\"Email\\",\\n    \\"password\\": \\"Password\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Usage in Components\\n\\n### Translation Hook\\n\\nUse the `useTranslation` hook to access translations:\\n\\n```tsx\\nimport { useTranslation } from \'react-i18next\';\\n\\nfunction MyComponent() {\\n  const { t } = useTranslation();\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      <h1>{t(\'login.title\')}</h1>\\n      <p>{t(\'common.messages.system_error\')}</p>\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Language Switching\\n\\nUse the `useLanguage` hook to change languages:\\n\\n```tsx\\nimport { useLanguage } from \'@/providers\';\\n\\nfunction LanguageSwitcher() {\\n  const { language, changeLanguage } = useLanguage();\\n\\n  return (\\n    <select\\n      value={language.code}\\n      onChange={(e) => changeLanguage(e.target.value)}\\n    >\\n      {languages.map((lang) => (\\n        <option key={lang.code} value={lang.code}>\\n          {lang.name}\\n        </option>\\n      ))}\\n    </select>\\n  );\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## RTL Support\\n\\nFor right-to-left languages like Arabic:\\n\\n1. **Direction is set automatically** when language changes\\n2. **Use Tailwind\'s RTL variants** for direction-specific styling:\\n\\n```tsx\\n// Flip icons in RTL mode\\n<ChevronRight className=\\"rtl:rotate-180\\" />\\n\\n// Adjust text alignment\\n<th className=\\"text-left rtl:text-right\\" />\\n```\\n\\n## Formatting Utilities\\n\\nSupastart provides formatting functions in `src/i18n/format.ts`:\\n\\n```typescript\\n// Date formatting (output: \\"Dec 7, 2023\\")\\nformatDate(new Date());\\n\\n// Date and time (output: \\"Dec 7, 2023, 11:41 PM\\")\\nformatDateTime(new Date());\\n\\n// Time only (output: \\"11:41 PM\\")\\nformatTime(new Date());\\n\\n// Currency (output: \\"$1,234.56\\")\\nformatMoney(1234.56, \'USD\');\\n```\\n\\n## Implementation\\n\\n### Language Provider\\n\\nThe `I18nProvider` manages language state and persists preferences:\\n\\n```tsx\\n// From src/providers/i18n-provider.tsx\\nfunction LanguageSwitcherExample() {\\n  const { language, changeLanguage } = useLanguage();\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      <p>Current: {language.name}</p>\\n      <button onClick={() => changeLanguage(\'en\')}>English</button>\\n      <button onClick={() => changeLanguage(\'ar\')}>Arabic (RTL)</button>\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Direction Provider\\n\\nThe `DirectionProvider` integrates with Radix UI for RTL support:\\n\\n```tsx\\n// src/providers/direction-provider.tsx\\nconst DirectionProvider = ({ children }) => {\\n  const { language } = useLanguage();\\n  return (\\n    <RadixDirectionProvider dir={language.direction}>\\n      {children}\\n    </RadixDirectionProvider>\\n  );\\n};\\n```","code":"var Component=(()=>{var p=Object.create;var a=Object.defineProperty;var E=Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor;var y=Object.getOwnPropertyNames;var g=Object.getPrototypeOf,m=Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty;var u=(l,n)=>()=>(n||l((n={exports:{}}).exports,n),n.exports),F=(l,n)=>{for(var s in n)a(l,s,{get:n[s],enumerable:!0})},c=(l,n,s,i)=>{if(n&&typeof n==\\"object\\"||typeof n==\\"function\\")for(let r of y(n))!m.call(l,r)&&r!==s&&a(l,r,{get:()=>n[r],enumerable:!(i=E(n,r